cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ADIT: Atomistic Design and Interpretation Toolkit"
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below, together with the simulation codes you ran."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The ADIT project"
repository-code: "https://github.com/adit-chem-project/adit-chem"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0a1
date-released: "2026-09-15"
abstract: >-
  A desktop application that prepares atomistic simulations and turns their results into
  figures and tables. It builds structures, writes complete input sets for DFTB+, VASP, xtb,
  Quantum ESPRESSO, ORCA, CP2K, LAMMPS, GROMACS and other codes, and analyses the output.
